          <output>`Task.run` completed for `org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.task.A02_UpdatePageSkeletons` (an `InstructionTask`).

## Execution trace

| Phase | Result |
|---|---|
| `prerequisites` | none defined → nothing enforced |
| `rules` | none defined → nothing applied |
| `execute()` | followed `instructions` (below) |
| `successCriteria` | none defined → single pass |

## What `execute()` did (per the task's `instructions`)

1. Read `a01_planning.data.BmlDocSetPlan` → 25 `PagePlan` entries (all under the `docs.` sub-package), each with `name` + `scopes`.
2. Created 25 page skeletons, one per `PagePlan`, extending `DocPage`.
3. Each skeleton has: `baseType`, `is`, `documentation` (derived from the plan's `scopes`), `references` to authoritative-source Blocks, and property overrides `title` / `purpose` (from `scopes`) / `detailLevel` / `pageType`.
4. No aggregations implemented (`content`, `scopes`, `exclusions`, `authoritativeSources`, etc. left for the a03 authoring stage).
5. `Library.bml` catalog + namespace updated (via `blockml new`) for all 25 blocks.

`npx blockml validate` → **90 blocks, 0 errors, 0 warnings** (only pre-existing-style `PREFER_MARKDOWN` recommendations, same as the a03 pages).

## Two deviations from the literal instruction text, resolved against the actual model

- **Target package**: instructions say `...a02_structuring.page.*`; used `org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.page.docs.*` — the pre-existing empty `a02_structuring/data/page/` directory, mirroring `a03_authoring.data.page.docs` and matching the `docs.`-prefixed `PagePlan` names relative to a `.data.page` base package.
- **Base type**: instructions say `org.blockml.bml.docgen.core.DocPage` (does not exist); used the real `org.blockml.bml.docgen.page.DocPage`, same as the a03 pages.

Also reverted an incidental `&lt;isNot>`→`&lt;isnot>` casing change that `blockml new` made to `Library.bml`.

Files are unstaged/untracked; no commit made.
